---

## Key Learning Outcomes

After completing Week 07, I developed a better understanding of:

- How VPNs provide secure remote access
- How VPN tunnelling and encryption protect network traffic
- The difference between remote-access and site-to-site VPNs
- Different VPN protocols such as IPsec, OpenVPN, SSL/TLS VPN and WireGuard
- The difference between IPsec Transport Mode and Tunnel Mode
- Full tunnelling and split tunnelling
- Security benefits and limitations of VPNs

---

## Reflection

Week 07 helped me understand the importance of VPNs in network security. The activities gave me practical knowledge of how VPN connections work and how different protocols can be used to protect communication over public networks.

I also learned that VPNs improve privacy and security but do not guarantee complete anonymity. Understanding different VPN protocols and tunnelling methods will help me make better security decisions when designing and managing networks.

---

